{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792580200340,"sessionID":"ses_ea1e4f3a4ffec6vTW6W3rx1miA","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"Dk1Ly8YMyu413LGH","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/tmp/hevo_ws/biostatisticians_task2_jb-oc-agg1__biostatisticians__task2__agg1_15572/task_folder/DX24_301_protocol_synopsis.csv"},"output":"<path>/tmp/hevo_ws/biostatisticians_task2_jb-oc-agg1__biostatisticians__task2__agg1_15572/task_folder/DX24_301_protocol_synopsis.csv</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: Parameter,Value\n2: Protocol Number,DX24-301\n3: Study Title,\"A Phase III, Randomized, Double-Blind, Placebo-Controlled Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of Drug X (a GLP-1 Receptor Agonist) in Patients with Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus Inadequately Controlled on Metformin\"\n4: Study Phase,Phase III\n5: Study Design,\"Randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, parallel-group\"\n6: Randomization Ratio,1:1 (Drug X : Placebo)\n7: Treatment Duration,24 weeks\n8: Primary Endpoint,Change from baseline in HbA1c at Week 24\n9: Key Secondary Endpoint 1,Change from baseline in fasting plasma glucose (FPG) at Week 24\n10: Key Secondary Endpoint 2,Change from baseline in body weight at Week 24\n11: Key Secondary Endpoint 3,Proportion of patients achieving HbA1c <7.0% at Week 24\n12: Other Secondary Endpoint 1,Change from baseline in systolic blood pressure at Week 24\n13: Other Secondary Endpoint 2,Change from baseline in LDL cholesterol at Week 24\n14: Target Population,Adults aged 18-75 years with T2D and HbA1c 7.0-10.5% on stable metformin\n15: Planned Enrollment,480 subjects (240 per arm)\n16: Number of Sites,25 sites across 5 countries\n17: Statistical Analysis - Primary,ANCOVA with treatment as factor and baseline HbA1c as covariate; ITT population with LOCF\n18: Statistical Analysis - Secondary (continuous),ANCOVA with treatment as factor and respective baseline value as covariate\n19: Statistical Analysis - Secondary (binary),Logistic regression with treatment as factor and baseline HbA1c as covariate\n20: Multiplicity Adjustment,Hierarchical testing for key secondary endpoints\n21: Alpha Level,Two-sided 0.05\n22: Power,90% for primary endpoint\n23: Assumed Treatment Difference (HbA1c),-1.0% (Drug X vs Placebo)\n24: Assumed Common SD (HbA1c change),1.2%\n25: Dropout Rate Assumed,10%\n26: Safety Assessments,\"Adverse events, vital signs, laboratory tests, hypoglycemic events\"\n27: Primary Analysis Population,Intent-to-treat (ITT) - all randomized subjects\n28: Sensitivity Analysis Population,Per-protocol (PP) - subjects completing 24 weeks without major protocol violations\n\n(End of file - total 28 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"Parameter,Value\nProtocol Number,DX24-301\nStudy Title,\"A Phase III, Randomized, Double-Blind, Placebo-Controlled Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of Drug X (a GLP-1 Receptor Agonist) in Patients with Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus Inadequately Controlled on Metformin\"\nStudy Phase,Phase III\nStudy Design,\"Randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, parallel-group\"\nRandomization Ratio,1:1 (Drug X : Placebo)\nTreatment Duration,24 weeks\nPrimary Endpoint,Change from baseline in HbA1c at Week 24\nKey Secondary Endpoint 1,Change from baseline in fasting plasma glucose (FPG) at Week 24\nKey Secondary Endpoint 2,Change from baseline in body weight at Week 24\nKey Secondary Endpoint 3,Proportion of patients achieving HbA1c <7.0% at Week 24\nOther Secondary Endpoint 1,Change from baseline in systolic blood pressure at Week 24\nOther Secondary Endpoint 2,Change from baseline in LDL cholesterol at Week 24\nTarget Population,Adults aged 18-75 years with T2D and HbA1c 7.0-10.5% on stable metformin\nPlanned Enrollment,480 subjects (240 per arm)\nNumber of Sites,25 sites across 5 countries\nStatistical Analysis - Primary,ANCOVA with treatment as factor and baseline HbA1c as covariate; ITT population with LOCF\nStatistical Analysis - Secondary (continuous),ANCOVA with treatment as factor and respective baseline value as covariate\nStatistical Analysis - Secondary (binary),Logistic regression with treatment as factor and baseline HbA1c as covariate\nMultiplicity Adjustment,Hierarchical testing for key secondary endpoints","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"tmp/hevo_ws/biostatisticians_task2_jb-oc-agg1__biostatisticians__task2__agg1_15572/task_folder/DX24_301_protocol_synopsis.csv","time":{"start":1792580200330,"end":1792580200339}},"id":"prt_15e1b2789001fyNaew3vSfijAk","sessionID":"ses_ea1e4f3a4ffec6vTW6W3rx1miA","messageID":"msg_15e1b17340010lHlwE5Xq7gChJ"}}
